  "result": "I wrote `tests/unit/intervals.test.ts` and ran `npx vitest run`: **12 tests pass and 4 fail.** The failures come from a bug in `src/intervals.ts`, not from the tests, and I didn't change the source file as you asked.\n\n**The bug:** The doc comment says the function merges blocks that \"overlap or touch,\" and that no two blocks in the result \"touch or overlap.\" But the check at `src/intervals.ts:17` is `start < last[1]`, so blocks that only share an endpoint are never merged. For example, `[[1,2],[2,3]]` comes back unchanged instead of as `[[1,3]]`.\n\n**The 4 failing tests**, all cases of blocks touching:\n- merges intervals that touch at an endpoint\n- merges a chain of touching intervals\n- merges a zero-length interval touching another\n- produces output where no two intervals touch or overlap\n\nChanging `<` to `<=` on line 17 should make all 16 pass. I haven't tried it, since that means editing the source.\n\n**Passing tests cover:** empty input, a single interval, separate intervals, overlapping intervals, one interval inside another, unsorted input, duplicates, zero-length intervals, negative numbers, that the input isn't changed, and that the result is made of new arrays rather than the input's.",
